Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:54:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the bottom screen for the remote touch screen, and its
 touches

The remote touch screen (PS5CEMU-HAR #38, from dolphin78's prototype)
shows the 3DS's bottom screen in a browser on the local network and
sends its touches back. While a browser shows it, the port asks for a
picture at most 30 times a second (AzaharPS5_StreamWantFrame): the
screenshot's staging-copy path draws the bottom screen alone at its own
320 x 240, without the stereo mode, the cursor or the port's overlays,
whether or not the TV's layout shows it, and hands the RGB rows to the
port (AzaharPS5_StreamFrame) instead of the screenshot's buffer. The
copy is made visible to the host before it is read.

EmuWindow::TouchNormalized touches the bottom screen at a point from 0
to 1 across it, whatever the TV's layout, for the browser's touches.
